Removes the "Programme Liability" report added in 3.3.31/3.3.32
Original JIRA ticket: IPET-3635

The report reads mst_rewards_liability_aggregated_hour, a table Mirasvit creates only inside Report\Points::_aggregateLiability() and never declares in any setup script (setup_version is still 1.0.42). iPet disables that aggregation on purpose (DisableAggregate plugin, IPET-2843 - it walks 10 years of history and hammers the DB), so the table never comes into existence and ReportApi\Config\Entity\Table::initFields() blows up on DESCRIBE for every admin request:
  SQLSTATE[42S02]: Base table or view not found: 1146 Table ..._liability_aggregated_hour does not exist

Unregisters the report instead of creating the table for them: the report table definition, the report pool entry and the admin menu item. Deliberately left with an open upper version bound so the next release that touches these lines fails the build and forces a re-review.

diff --git a/src/RewardsAdminUi/etc/mst_report.xml b/src/RewardsAdminUi/etc/mst_report.xml
--- a/src/RewardsAdminUi/etc/mst_report.xml
+++ b/src/RewardsAdminUi/etc/mst_report.xml
@@ -34,18 +34,4 @@
         <column name="pushnotification_signup" label="Earned for push notifications sign up" type="number"/>
         <column name="referred_customer_signup" label="Earned for referred customer sign up" type="number"/>
     </table>
-
-    <table name="mst_rewards_liability_aggregated_hour">
-        <fk name="customer_id" table="customer_entity"/>
-
-        <column name="period" label="Period" type="date"/>
-
-        <column name="store_id" label="Store" type="store"/>
-        <column name="customer_group_id" label="Customer Groups" type="select" options="Magento\Customer\Model\ResourceModel\Group\Collection"/>
-
-        <column name="points_earned" label="Earned" type="number"/>
-        <column name="points_redeemed" label="Redeemed" type="number"/>
-        <column name="points_expired" label="Expired" type="number"/>
-        <column name="balance_delta" label="Outstanding (net)" type="number"/>
-    </table>
 </config>
